# Compiled Python bytecode. 26 of these were tracked under tools/agentkit until
# 3 September 2026. They are build output: regenerated on import, named for the
# interpreter that wrote them (cpython-311, and CI runs 3.12), and they go stale
# the moment a .py beside them changes. CPython validates the source mtime and
# size before using a cached .pyc, so a stale one is recompiled rather than
# silently executed -- this is repository hygiene, not a correctness fix, and
# the distinction is worth keeping straight.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Written by scripts/audit-dependencies.mjs on every run, and uploaded by
# dependency-scan.yml as a CI artifact. Nothing reads it out of the repository.
#
# It was committed by accident on 3 September 2026, during the npm advisory
# outage, so the tracked copy was an EMPTY file -- which is the "could not ask"
# state that scripts/audit-result-is-unusable.mjs exists to detect, frozen into
# a fresh checkout. Harmless, because the audit overwrites it before that check
# reads it, but a build artifact in source is noise at best.
pnpm-audit.json
